# Do Not Run Code Without Explicit Request

Do **not** run the Processor or HtmlScrapper unless the user **explicitly** asks you to run them.

## Allowed without explicit request

- `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` when verifying changes during implementation or CI fixes.
- Read-only inspection (`git status`, `git log`, reading files, grep).

## Requires explicit user request

- `dotnet run` on Processor or HtmlScrapper.
- Full pipeline runs against real data paths (e.g. `HistoricalWeatherFilesRoot`).
- Any long-running or data-producing execution outside build/test.

When verification needs a pipeline run, **ask first** or wait until the user says to run it.
